WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:07.810
After eight seasons and 10 years on the air,
Game of Thrones came to a surprising and controversial

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:08.810
end.

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:14.850
We're here to rank its major characters' endings
from worst to best -- and boy, there are some

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:15.850
doozies.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:21.119
Introduced in the third season as a slave,
Missandei is quickly welcomed into Daenerys

00:00:21.119 --> 00:00:23.699
Targaryen's camp as a free woman.

00:00:23.699 --> 00:00:28.869
The two soon become close friends and confidantes,
rarely leaving each other's side throughout

00:00:28.869 --> 00:00:30.419
much of the series.

00:00:30.419 --> 00:00:35.920
However, in the show's final season, when
Daenerys' ships are attacked, Missandei is

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:41.070
captured by the allied forces of Euron Greyjoy
and Cersei Lannister.

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:46.190
When Daenerys tries to save her friend, the
duo beheads Missandei in front of the desperate

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:48.040
dragon queen.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:53.720
Missandei's death is tragic, and her last
word proves her loyalty to Daenerys with gutting

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.220
finality.

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:56.720
"Dracarys."

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:02.210
Although Missandei using Daenerys' catchphrase
was powerful, her death was in poor taste.

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:08.030
One of the show's few characters of color,
Missandei was a thoughtful, layered character

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:13.450
who was needlessly killed off simply to motivate
Daenerys in the show's final few episodes.

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:19.909
One of the show's most sinister villains,
Cersei Lannister looms large over Game of

00:01:19.909 --> 00:01:25.939
Thrones, from her affair with her twin brother
Jaime to her abject cruelty towards her enemies.

00:01:25.939 --> 00:01:31.049
One would think that a complex character like
Cersei would get an ending befitting her impressive

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:32.049
legacy.

00:01:32.049 --> 00:01:35.490
But unfortunately, that doesn't come to pass.

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:40.909
In the final season, Cersei ends up in the
line of fire when Daenerys arrives at King's

00:01:40.909 --> 00:01:42.999
Landing, dragon blazing.

00:01:42.999 --> 00:01:48.860
As Cersei's home base collapses in rubble,
the typically inscrutable queen is alone until

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:50.420
her brother, Jaime, arrives.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:56.030
The two die together, crushed under falling
debris as they attempt to escape.

00:01:56.030 --> 00:02:00.950
This ending proved to be pretty disappointing
for fans who expected the ruthless queen to

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:03.409
go out in a more dramatic fashion.

00:02:04.409 --> 00:02:10.310
Over the course of the series, Jaime Lannister
becomes one of the show's most complex characters.

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:16.220
After beginning the series loyal to Cersei,
Jaime eventually turns away from his sister,

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:19.900
deciding to help his brother Tyrion and Daenerys
instead.

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:25.570
But at the end of the series, Jaime returns
to Cersei, right after finally consummating

00:02:25.570 --> 00:02:29.540
his slow-burn relationship with Brienne of
Tarth.

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:35.680
Ultimately, Jaime rejects his honorable path
to die alongside Cersei in the Red Keep.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:40.489
Though it makes poetic sense that the duo
would leave the world together, it felt as

00:02:40.489 --> 00:02:46.500
though Jaime's anticlimactic ending undermined
many seasons of impressive character growth.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:53.380
As one of the most popular and beloved characters
on the small screen, many fans fully expected

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:59.260
Daenerys, the Mother of Dragons, to take the
Iron Throne by the end of the series.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:03.840
Unfortunately, Daenerys had a far different
fate waiting for her.

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:09.900
Upon conquering King's Landing, Daenerys loses
control of her emotions and lays waste to

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:13.540
the city, killing countless innocent civilians.

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:17.310
Even her closest allies realize she must be
stopped.

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:22.920
Before she can take the Iron Throne, Daenerys'
lover Jon Snow kills his queen for the good

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:24.180
of the realm.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:30.470
In the wake of her death, her last remaining
dragon, Drogon, torches the Throne and carries

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:32.250
his mother away.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:37.750
Daenerys' ending is certainly dramatic, but
her sudden descent into madness and rushed

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:41.519
death tarnish her character's otherwise incredible
story.

00:03:42.519 --> 00:03:47.209
From the very first scene of Game of Thrones,
viewers are made aware that despite rampant

00:03:47.209 --> 00:03:52.959
infighting within the Seven Kingdoms, the
realm has a bigger threat looming: the ancient

00:03:52.959 --> 00:03:56.640
and mysterious beings known as White Walkers.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:01.450
Though the Night's Watch guards the northern
Wall to try and protect Westeros from what

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:07.099
lies beyond, the White Walkers start heading
south in the show's second season.

00:04:07.099 --> 00:04:12.689
When the show's heroes finally face off against
the Night King and his army, all hope seems

00:04:12.689 --> 00:04:13.689
lost.

00:04:13.689 --> 00:04:19.299
However, just when the humans have all but
given up, Arya Stark leaps from the darkness

00:04:19.299 --> 00:04:22.220
and kills the Night King once and for all.

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:27.640
While this makes for an epic moment, it's
also weirdly disappointing: After years of

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:32.990
mystery surrounding the Night King, his entire
storyline ends in seconds.

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:38.000
The Night King was set up as a major villain,
but ultimately, the show disposes of him like

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.810
a minor baddie.

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:45.389
It's hard not to feel cheated out of a potentially
gripping story about this intriguing character.

00:04:46.389 --> 00:04:51.810
Few of Game of Thrones' conniving characters
had as much potential as Margaery Tyrell,

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:57.460
an unparalleled strategist who was also the
prize beauty of the wealthy House Tyrell.

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:03.729
After a short-lived marriage to Renly Baratheon,
Margaery shifts her allegiances to the Lannister

00:05:03.729 --> 00:05:06.389
family in King's Landing.

00:05:06.389 --> 00:05:12.479
Before long, Margaery is married to the sadistic
Joffrey Baratheon, but when he is assassinated

00:05:12.479 --> 00:05:18.460
at their wedding, she ends up serving as queen
to his sweet younger brother, Tommen.

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:24.160
Unfortunately for Margaery, however, she makes
an enemy of Cersei almost immediately thanks

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:26.650
to her beauty and quick mind.

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:32.081
When Cersei vindictively blows up the Sept
of Baelor before she can be tried for her

00:05:32.081 --> 00:05:36.099
various crimes, Margaery is among her many
victims.

00:05:36.099 --> 00:05:41.360
Although Margaery realizes what's happening
before Cersei's plan is executed, she's unable

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:47.500
to escape in time, bringing her fascinating
story to an abrupt and disappointing conclusion.

00:05:48.599 --> 00:05:54.449
After being paralyzed by Jaime Lannister in
the show's first episode, Bran Stark gradually

00:05:54.449 --> 00:06:01.289
grows into someone entirely new, taking on
the mantle of the omniscient Three-Eyed Raven.

00:06:01.289 --> 00:06:06.379
When Westeros needs to choose a new king in
the wake of Daenerys' death, Tyrion makes

00:06:06.379 --> 00:06:09.949
a surprising case for Bran to take the throne.

00:06:09.949 --> 00:06:14.250
Despite previous assertions from Bran that
he has no political ambitions for himself…

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:16.460
"I could never be lord of anything.

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:18.000
I'm the Three-Eyed Raven."

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:21.940
Bran is somehow chosen as the next King of
Westeros.

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:27.550
The reasons that put him on the throne are
nonsensical at best, bringing the series-long

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:32.500
struggle for the Iron Throne to a frustrating
and unsatisfying conclusion.

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:38.810
A master of gossip and intrigue, Varys spends
the series frequently teaming up with fellow

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:45.240
strategists like Petyr "Littlefinger" Baelish
and Tyrion to advance his political career

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:47.310
and the cause of peace in Westeros.

00:06:47.310 --> 00:06:53.250
For most of the show, there's rarely any doubt
that Varys always has a brilliant plan up

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:54.740
his sleeve.

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:59.750
Unfortunately, Varys' potential is wildly
squandered by the time the show draws to a

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:00.790
close.

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:06.051
After doing very little in the last two seasons,
he acts completely out of character when he

00:07:06.051 --> 00:07:10.080
stages an open, obvious coup against Daenerys.

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:15.800
Unsurprisingly, his scheme is uncovered, and
Daenerys executes him for treason, resulting

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:20.860
in an utterly unsatisfying ending for one
of the show's most intriguing characters.

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:26.889
Introduced as a perpetually frightened brother
of the Night's Watch, Samwell Tarly eventually

00:07:26.889 --> 00:07:32.180
proves himself in battle, and spends time
expanding his knowledge at the Citadel.

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:38.259
Though Sam finds himself rejected by his noble
family, his growth as a character is pretty

00:07:38.259 --> 00:07:39.280
impressive.

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:44.470
At the conclusion of Game of Thrones, Sam
is shown wearing Maesters robes, indicating

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:47.639
he is now one of the intellectual elite.

00:07:47.639 --> 00:07:51.470
It turns out he has been named the Grandmaester
for King Bran.

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:56.310
He also writes a book that chronicles the
dramatic events of the series, and settles

00:07:56.310 --> 00:08:00.760
down with Gilly and Sam Jr., their young son.

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:06.290
Sam's ending might be unusually neat and tidy
for Game of Thrones, but he deserves a happy

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:07.680
ending.

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:13.979
Theon Greyjoy begins Game of Thrones as the
insecure ward of the Stark family who overtakes

00:08:13.979 --> 00:08:17.210
Winterfell the second the family departs.

00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:22.750
However, Theon ends up suffering for his crimes
when he's captured by the Bolton clan and

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:27.100
tortured by Roose Bolton's sadistic son, Ramsay.

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:33.219
Before long, Theon has lost his grasp on his
former identity, referring to himself only

00:08:33.219 --> 00:08:34.570
as "Reek."

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:41.219
Reek endures horrific torture, but eventually,
Theon's bravery returns, as does his loyalty

00:08:41.219 --> 00:08:43.050
to the Stark family.

00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:48.959
After helping Sansa Stark escape Ramsay's
captivity, Theon volunteers to personally

00:08:48.959 --> 00:08:52.150
guard Bran during the Battle of Winterfell.

00:08:52.150 --> 00:08:57.940
Ultimately, Theon sacrifices himself to save
Bran, providing redemption for one of the

00:08:57.940 --> 00:09:01.710
show's most complicated and long-suffering
characters.

00:09:02.710 --> 00:09:08.060
From the beginning, it's clear that Jorah
Mormont harbors romantic feelings for Daenerys,

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:10.080
the young Mother of Dragons.

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:15.520
After meeting Daenerys at her wedding to Dothraki
warrior Khal Drogo, the disgraced heir of

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:21.570
the Mormont clan pledges his loyalty to his
Khaleesi, and stands by her side until the

00:09:21.570 --> 00:09:22.930
bitter end.

00:09:22.930 --> 00:09:28.160
During the Battle of Winterfell, Jorah tries
his best to defend his Khaleesi, and gets

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:30.880
mortally wounded in the process.

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:36.090
Not only does Jorah nobly sacrifice himself
for his queen, but he escapes having to see

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:40.730
Daenerys abandon her principles during her
attack on King's Landing.

00:09:40.730 --> 00:09:46.030
In a way, this gives Jorah the best ending
he could hope for.

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:52.320
Sandor "The Hound" Clegane became a fan favorite
early on, thanks to his gruff demeanor, fighting

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:55.120
prowess, and secret sensitive side.

00:09:55.120 --> 00:10:01.200
His scarred face is courtesy of his brother,
Gregor "The Mountain" Clegane, who shoved

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:04.750
Sandor into a fire when they were both young.

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:10.459
The Hound doesn't care about much, but he
does care about getting revenge on his brother.

00:10:10.459 --> 00:10:15.260
Eventually, the Hound forms a close bond with
Arya Stark.

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:20.639
As one of his final acts, he saves her life
by convincing her to flee a crumbling King's

00:10:20.639 --> 00:10:21.639
Landing.

00:10:21.639 --> 00:10:26.600
But rather than escape with her, the Hound
faces off against his brother, who has become

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:28.340
an unstoppable killing machine.

00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:35.000
Ultimately, the Cleganes die together when
the Hound flings them both into the flames

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:38.880
below, giving him a tragic but poetically
fitting ending

00:10:40.130 --> 00:10:46.260
A fighter of uncommon skill, dedication, and
honor, Brienne of Tarth's refusal to adhere

00:10:46.260 --> 00:10:51.010
to traditional gender roles often makes her
feel like an outsider.

00:10:51.010 --> 00:10:56.190
Desperate to prove her worth in battle, she
eventually allies herself with the Stark family,

00:10:56.190 --> 00:11:00.920
promising to protect Sansa and Arya as well
as she can.

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:05.680
Along the way, Brienne also forms an intense
bond with Jaime Lannister.

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:10.860
He knights Brienne before the Battle of Winterfell,
making her the first female knight of the

00:11:10.860 --> 00:11:12.500
Seven Kingdoms.

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:17.940
When they both survive the attack, Jaime and
Brienne consummate their relationship.

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:23.440
Unfortunately, Jaime ends up abandoning Brienne
for Cersei shortly thereafter.

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:28.450
Though Brienne is left bereft, the blow is
softened when she becomes Lord Commander of

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:34.830
the Kingsguard, fulfilling her destiny as
one of Westeros' most formidable and honorable

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:35.830
warriors.

00:11:36.830 --> 00:11:42.040
Serving as the Stark family's servant, the
lovable giant Hodor manages to find emotional

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:48.240
nuances with each repetition of his name,
which is the only word he is able to say.

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:53.800
For a long time, viewers have no idea why
Hodor has such a limited vocabulary, until

00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:58.410
season six's "The Door" reveals his shocking
backstory.

00:11:58.410 --> 00:12:02.940
As Bran gains the knowledge to become the
Three Eyed Raven, who can travel throughout

00:12:02.940 --> 00:12:08.660
space and time, he encounters a young Hodor,
who has a full vocabulary.

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:14.480
However, while Bran is in the past, wights
attack the present-day Bran and Hodor.

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:20.139
Hodor blocks the wights behind a door so Bran
can escape, while in the past, a young Hodor

00:12:20.139 --> 00:12:31.899
yells one sentence over and over, until it
turns into a single word:

00:12:31.899 --> 00:12:50.320
"Hold the door," repeated until it's "Hodor"

00:12:50.320 --> 00:12:56.290
Losing Hodor is heartbreaking, but the revelation
of his past is an incredible feat of storytelling.

00:12:57.290 --> 00:13:03.700
While violent, charming Wildling Tormund Giantsbane
was initially no big fan of Jon Snow, the

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:10.170
two eventually become close friends, fighting
alongside one another time and time again.

00:13:10.170 --> 00:13:14.610
Tormund ends up surviving the battle against
the White Walkers as well as the siege of

00:13:14.610 --> 00:13:15.970
King's Landing.

00:13:15.970 --> 00:13:21.630
Though his enormous crush on Brienne remains
unrequited, Tormund's ending is fitting, with

00:13:21.630 --> 00:13:27.331
him returning to the far North where he belongs,
alongside his sworn brother, Jon Snow.

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:35.079
One of Game of Thrones' most emotionally conflicted
characters, Jon Snow always wants to do what's

00:13:35.079 --> 00:13:36.079
right.

00:13:36.079 --> 00:13:41.500
That instinct leaves him with a hard decision
to make when his lover, Daenerys, decimates

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:43.480
the city of King's Landing.

00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:50.730
After talking to Tyrion, Jon realizes he must
do the right thing despite his love for Daenerys.

00:13:50.730 --> 00:13:56.620
As the Dragon Queen reaches the Iron Throne
she has fought so hard to win, Jon stabs her

00:13:56.620 --> 00:13:57.960
in the chest.

00:13:57.960 --> 00:14:04.290
After Dany's death, Drogon burns the throne
and carries Dany away, but Jon still must

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:06.620
face justice for his crime.

00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:12.920
Eventually, it's decided that Jon will be
banished from Westeros and return to the North.

00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:18.370
Though this is painted as punishment, it feels
natural for Jon Snow, who never felt at home

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:21.740
in the halls of the kings and queens of Westeros.

00:14:21.740 --> 00:14:27.060
He heads back into the Northern wilderness
with Tormund and his loyal direwolf, Ghost,

00:14:27.060 --> 00:14:28.060
by his side.

00:14:29.060 --> 00:14:34.959
Born without a prestigious name, Petyr Baelish
quickly learned to do anything to gain power.

00:14:34.959 --> 00:14:41.330
Eventually, the conniving noble known as Littlefinger
became a major player within King's Landing,

00:14:41.330 --> 00:14:46.310
running a brothel and collecting information
on the biggest names in Westeros.

00:14:46.310 --> 00:14:52.101
Though he seemed loyal to Sansa Stark, he
readily traded her to Ramsay Bolton when he

00:14:52.101 --> 00:14:54.520
thought it might gain him power.

00:14:54.520 --> 00:15:01.800
Once Sansa returns to Winterfell, Littlefinger
does his very best to pit sister against sister,

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:05.320
attempting to turn Sansa and Arya against
one another.

00:15:05.320 --> 00:15:10.360
Though Littlefinger thinks victory is nigh
when Sansa calls for a trial that he assumes

00:15:10.360 --> 00:15:13.500
is for Arya, she beats him at his own game.

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:16.150
"You stand accused of treason.

00:15:16.150 --> 00:15:22.840
How do you answer these charges, Lord Baelish?"

00:15:22.840 --> 00:15:28.750
On Sansa's orders, Arya slits his throat,
and Littlefinger's death provides an incredibly

00:15:28.750 --> 00:15:32.370
satisfying ending for this often despicable
man.

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:38.350
For a show with its fair share of bad guys,
few are as repulsive as Ramsay Bolton.

00:15:38.350 --> 00:15:44.790
In addition to tormenting Theon, Ramsay repeatedly
assaulted Sansa Stark and killed her younger

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:47.820
brother Rickon just for fun.

00:15:47.820 --> 00:15:49.720
After he kills Rickon.

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:55.160
Ramsay loses the Battle of the Bastards, and
finds himself at the mercy of the surviving

00:15:55.160 --> 00:15:56.310
Starks.

00:15:56.310 --> 00:16:02.370
Bound and helpless in the depths of Winterfell,
Ramsay sneers at Sansa until he realizes that

00:16:02.370 --> 00:16:05.970
he's surrounded by his own snarling dogs.

00:16:05.970 --> 00:16:10.899
When Ramsay says they'll never hurt him, Sansa
points out that Ramsay stopped feeding them

00:16:10.899 --> 00:16:15.480
days prior, in anticipation of winning the
battle.

00:16:15.480 --> 00:16:20.230
He'd been planning to feed the Starks to his
pets, as he'd done with other victims in the

00:16:20.230 --> 00:16:21.269
past.

00:16:21.269 --> 00:16:26.790
As Sansa leaves him to the same fate he'd
dealt out to so many others, Ramsay's dogs

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:32.360
rip him to shreds, putting an end to Game
of Thrones' most reprehensible sociopath.

00:16:33.959 --> 00:16:39.050
Tyrion Lannister goes on a winding journey
throughout Game of Thrones, but ends up right

00:16:39.050 --> 00:16:40.630
where he should be.

00:16:40.630 --> 00:16:45.810
After facing imprisonment for turning on Daenerys
after her siege of King's Landing, Tyrion

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:50.649
convinces Jon to assassinate Daenerys for
the good of the realm.

00:16:50.649 --> 00:16:55.069
Despite her allies being furious with him,
Tyrion is still brought to the council that

00:16:55.069 --> 00:17:01.480
will decide the fate of Westeros' monarchy,
and actually ends up handpicking the new King.

00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:07.420
Bran chooses Tyrion to serve as Hand of the
King -- a job he doesn't initially want, after

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:09.610
having served as Hand before.

00:17:09.610 --> 00:17:14.060
But the truth is that pulling the strings
behind a leader is where Tyrion's strengths

00:17:14.060 --> 00:17:16.080
can best be utilized.

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:22.580
The last scene of the series sees Tyrion comfortably
leading one of Bran's Small Council meetings,

00:17:22.580 --> 00:17:24.950
proving that he's exactly where he belongs.

00:17:26.170 --> 00:17:30.800
After using the faceless assassin skills that
she acquired throughout the series to seek

00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:37.230
revenge against her enemies and defeat the
Night King, Arya Stark deserves a break.

00:17:37.230 --> 00:17:42.230
But with the wars in Westeros drawing to a
close and demand dwindling for her hard-won

00:17:42.230 --> 00:17:47.920
fighting skills, Arya is faced with the daunting
decision about what to do with the rest of

00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:48.990
her life.

00:17:48.990 --> 00:17:54.680
Ultimately, Arya sets off to explore the world,
telling her brothers and sister that she wants

00:17:54.680 --> 00:17:57.150
to find "what's west of Westeros."

00:17:57.150 --> 00:18:02.920
Armed with her trusty sword, Needle, Arya
sets sail to explore the darkest corners of

00:18:02.920 --> 00:18:09.190
the world, seeking independence outside the
contentious borders of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:13.890
Arya was always a character who sought her
own path in life, so to see her continuing

00:18:13.890 --> 00:18:19.110
to challenge herself and push boundaries is
a rewarding end for this beloved character.

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:24.830
One of the overarching messages of Game of
Thrones always seemed to be that the ideal

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:30.100
leader of the Seven Kingdoms would have the
cunning strategy of Cersei with the honor

00:18:30.100 --> 00:18:32.920
and trustworthiness of Jon Snow.

00:18:32.920 --> 00:18:38.960
So it was surprising and a little bit frustrating
when Sansa Stark, the character who most embodies

00:18:38.960 --> 00:18:43.540
both qualities, is overlooked in favor of
her brother, Bran.

00:18:43.540 --> 00:18:49.800
However, when Bran becomes King, the shrewd
Sansa seizes that opportunity to make an important

00:18:49.800 --> 00:18:50.800
request.

00:18:50.800 --> 00:18:56.320
"The North will remain an independent kingdom,
as it was for thousands of years."

00:18:56.320 --> 00:19:00.480
Bran agrees, and Sansa is rewarded for her
efforts.

00:19:00.480 --> 00:19:05.960
In one of the very last shots of the series,
viewers watch as Sansa is crowned the Queen

00:19:05.960 --> 00:19:11.960
in the North, ensuring that a Stark will remain
in Winterfell for years to come.

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:17.310
Though she would undoubtedly have been a fair
and capable ruler of Westeros, her home in

00:19:17.310 --> 00:19:22.980
the North is where she truly wants to be,
which makes her ending the perfect conclusion

00:19:22.980 --> 00:19:25.660
to her impressive tale.

00:19:26.810 --> 00:19:31.320
Olenna Tyrell, the matriarch of the wealthy
House Tyrell who carries the title of "Queen

00:19:31.320 --> 00:19:37.040
of Thorns," is known for always being several
steps ahead of everyone else.

00:19:37.040 --> 00:19:42.580
Her razor wit and even sharper tongue serve
her well throughout the series, and her final

00:19:42.580 --> 00:19:44.890
moments are no exception.

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:50.400
After allying herself with Daenerys and her
forces, Olenna finds herself outmatched against

00:19:50.400 --> 00:19:56.000
the Lannister armies as they approach her
home of Highgarden, leaving her trapped.

00:19:56.000 --> 00:20:02.060
Unwilling to violently slay an old woman,
Jaime gives her a poisoned glass of wine instead

00:20:02.060 --> 00:20:05.830
— but Olenna has one last trick up her sleeve.

00:20:05.830 --> 00:20:11.210
After drinking the poison, Olenna finally
reveals to Jaime that she is responsible for

00:20:11.210 --> 00:20:15.320
the death of his son with Cersei, the illegitimate
King Joffrey.

00:20:15.320 --> 00:20:16.420
"Tell Cersei.

00:20:16.420 --> 00:20:20.840
I want her to know it was me."

00:20:20.840 --> 00:20:25.850
Even though Jamie technically gets what he
wants by taking out one of his biggest enemies,

00:20:25.850 --> 00:20:32.510
Olenna still manages to come out on top, giving
her the best ending in all of Game of Thrones.

00:20:32.510 --> 00:20:34.930
As showrunner Dan Weiss once put it,

00:20:34.930 --> 00:20:37.880
"She beats him in the middle of her own death
scene."

